@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_connect_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - native connection acceptance

start
:Enter ProcessConnect from the engine's native open callback\nThe native server attributes are locked by that caller;
:ConnectClientInfo(ctp->info.scoid, client info, 0);
if (Client-info lookup fails?) then (yes)
    :Log ConnectClientInfo error and return EINVAL;
    stop
else (identity available)
    :Build ClientIdentity from request pid and effective uid/gid;
endif
:Allocate ServerConnection with the engine memory resource\nA local unique pointer owns the pending object;
:Construct identity and outgoing storage\nUserData and self_ remain empty;
:Invoke connect_callback_ with the pending connection;
note right
    Native OCB attachment has not happened yet.
    Notify can queue without an active select/ping event.
    AcceptConnection has not installed UserData.
end note
if (Connect callback returns an error?) then (yes)
    :Log connect_callback error;
    :Return EACCES\nThe local owner destroys the pending connection;
    stop
else (accepted by application)
    :engine_->AttachConnection(ctp, msg, server, connection);
endif
if (Native attachment returns an error?) then (yes)
    :Log AttachConnection error;
    :Return that native status\nThe local owner destroys the pending connection;
    stop
else (OCB bound)
    :AcceptConnection(move UserData, move local owner)\nStore user_data_, then transfer ownership to self_;
endif
:Return EOK;
stop

legend
    This view follows normal native request dispatch on the server worker.
    Allocation, application admission and OCB attachment are distinct steps.
    No catch/recovery or default-callback fallback is introduced.
    GetServer-based access depends on native binding; identity is already stored.
endlegend

@enduml
